    "notes": "Served with the OpenZeka DGX Spark recipe for Qwen3.8-27B (blog post \"Qwen3.8-27B on DGX Spark - 48 tok/s\", https://blog.openzeka.com/en/qwen3-8-27b-on-dgx-spark-48-tok-s/, published 2026-08-25), whose sparkrun recipe file qwen38-27b-dflash2.yaml was saved verbatim from the post and launched with the command given in the post, sparkrun 0.3.4 run qwen38-27b-dflash2.yaml --rootful --no-follow --no-rm, plus --hosts localhost because no default sparkrun cluster exists on this machine and --port 8888 instead of 8000. Image registry.cordata.ai/spark-cluster/sglang-qwen38-27b-dflash2:latest as published (repo digest sha256:2686b330, created 2026-08-25, SGLang 0.0.0.dev0+qwen38.27b.g561c8f3, torch 2.13.0+cu130). Target RadixArk/Qwen3.8-27B-NVFP4-BF16-LMHead at main 009632fe (the recipe pins no revision), DFlash2 speculative decoding against z-lab/Qwen3.8-27B-DFlash2 at revision 50307d4c, unquantized, with 8 draft tokens, mem-fraction-static 0.50, KV cache fp8_e4m3, bf16 mamba SSM state with mamba-full-memory-ratio 4.21 and 64 state slots, mamba radix cache extra_buffer, max-running-requests 16 (capped to 12 by the server), FlashInfer attention with autotune left on, chunked prefill 8192, prefill CUDA graph off, torch.compile off, stream-interval 1, sampling-defaults model and the native 262144 context window. The chat template comes from the target repository, so the served default is thinking on: the speed rows force thinking off per request with chat_template_kwargs enable_thinking false, the eval rows use that served default. The server runs without an API key; the harness attached over HTTP on 127.0.0.1:8888 and sent a bearer header the server ignores."
